    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d449">

                <pb facs="0555" n="1389" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1389"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/133a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-15T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 15, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6252. For Sheldon from
                    War Trade Board:</p>
                <p>Your No. 21, 12th. We agree to Dutch proposal with following slight changes: Of
                    the 150,000 tons, part to be employed in Belgian Relief, part to be used for
                    supplying Switzerland, which is cargo <pb facs="0556" n="1390" xml:id="pg1390"/>
                    under safe conduct, remaining tonnage to be used in trades outside Europe and
                    Atlantic islands. We are willing to allow the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Samarinda</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Adonis</hi> to go forward, or
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Zeelandia</hi> in substitution for either one of
                    them, upon understanding that equivalent amount of tonnage will be dispatched
                    from Holland at same time. Sorry cannot agree to release of four remaining
                    vessels mentioned your cable. The two vessels coming from Holland must be
                    assigned to trades outside Europe and Atlantic islands, the same as tonnage
                    first above mentioned. Hope you will obtain two round trips instead of one if
                    operated in short voyage trade, but we are not insisting upon this now.
                    Telegraph immediately in order to get the matter concluded.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
